# Pachelbel, Canon in D: the complete first-violin line (57 bars), reduced for piano over
# the two-bar ground bass. Violins II and III, which play the same line two and four bars
# later, are not included; the piano versions are generated reductions of these two parts.
# Bars 1-54 are from the oldest surviving source, a manuscript score copied ca. 1838-42
# (Staatsbibliothek zu Berlin, Mus.ms. 16481/8, IMSLP #346264), checked bar by bar.
# The manuscript breaks off after bar 54. Bars 55-57 are from Max Seiffert's edition
# (Organum III/24, Kistner & Siegel, 1929, IMSLP #44549), made from an old set of parts;
# only its violin notes are used, not its dynamics, articulation or keyboard realization.
# Seiffert's violin I also agrees with every manuscript bar. The trills in bars 10 and 40
# are left out (the source format has no ornaments); the notes they sit on are kept.
# The chord symbols are our reading of the ground bass; the continuo has no figures here.
title: Canon in D
piece: canon-in-d
added: 2026-10-17
source: public-domain
composer: Johann Pachelbel
composer-died: 1706
first-published: 1919
edition: Manuscript score, ca. 1838-42, Staatsbibliothek zu Berlin, Mus.ms. 16481/8 (IMSLP #346264), bars 1-54; Organum III/24, Kistner & Siegel, Leipzig, 1929 (IMSLP #44549), bars 55-57
editor: Max Seiffert
editor-died: 1948
editor-additions: not used
key: D major
meter: 4/4
# The manuscript has no tempo mark; the tempo is ours.
tempo: 64
summary: Pachelbel's canon: the whole first-violin line over the eight-note ground bass.
figure: held
medium-figure: held
# The opening eighth-note arpeggios stay as written in Easy; the generator merges the
# faster variations into the beat.
easy-keep: 5, 6

[Ground] 1-2
melody: | r:4 | r:4 |
chords: | D A Bm F#m | G D G A |
left: | D3q A2 B2 F#2 | G2q D2 G2 A2 |

